  "result": "Fixed. In `src/click/formatting.py`, `join_options` sorted an option's names with `reverse=True`, so `--help` output listed long names before short ones (`--verbose, -v`). I removed `reverse=True`, so short names now come first, as in upstream Click.\n\nOutput for a sample command now reads:\n\n```\nOptions:\n  -v, --verbose    x\n  -n, --name TEXT  y\n  --help           Show this message and exit.\n```\n\nThe existing test suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\nI interpreted \"weird order\" as the ordering of names within each option. If you meant something else, such as the order of the options themselves or the separate \"Positional arguments\" section this repo adds, tell me and I'll look at that instead.",
